[00:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Hey, my name is Fabian and I\'m the maker of AtlasVT, which is a completely free and open-source plug-in for Obsidian.md to turn your markdown world into an actual virtual tabletop. I\'ve been using Obsidian for world building and for'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'managing my campaigns for quite a while now. And while it\'s always been an incredible tool with birectional linking and plugins such as fantasy stat blocks which enables you to actually create stat blocks for various different game'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'systems within Obsidian. I have not ever really liked to switch from Obsidian to something like Albear or um Foundry and so on because um I don\'t like the context switching and I don\'t'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'like that my my maps and my notes and so on are kind of in two places where they cannot reach each other. Um and so I\'ve built this plug-in to make managing my campaigns and my sessions less stressful'

[00:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and more fun at the table. I just want to give you a quick overview of what you can expect from this plug-in um before I then go into the details of what kind of um premises I built this on and so on.'

[01:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Um but for now, you can see we have a map open here. Um it\'s super performant and fast. Uh it\'s all local on your um device and nothing ever leaves it. There'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is no ads, there is no AI features, there is no telemetry, it\'s just your stuff and that\'s it. Uh, you\'ve got an additional tab bar for the different'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'maps that you have within your different collections. You have widgets over here, a toolbar with stuff like fog of war, a draw tool, text measure, and stuff like uh dice. You can also um pin'

[01:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'uh notes to your maps. And for me, this is a super important feature. You can give it an icon here. You can either link to a specific heading or to the'

[01:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'entire file. And then [music] you can uh as you can see here, you can move it around. And you can click uh hold down command or control to open a preview of the file. Um you can also pin it and'

[02:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'move that around. um change the size and then even go ahead and like uh edit the file within it which is super fun um for managing or like preparing your'

[02:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sessions. Uh you can link to other maps for example. Um you can link to notes, you can use slash commands, you could do everything in here that you would uh in'

[02:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'any other kind of Obsidian note. And the coolest thing about it, I feel like, is when you switch to different maps and then you go back, it\'ll stay in that exact position where you left it. And this, I think, is a real game changer for preparing your sessions. At least it'

[02:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is for me. Uh, you can also, as I said, link to other maps. Um, we can see here that if we hover over them with command t down, we can see a preview and you can'

[03:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'click on open to open it. And that way you can kind of nest your maps within one another. Um, which is I think a super cool uh feature for preparing your world and managing it and getting an'

[03:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'idea of it yourself. Um, to see it in this kind of hierarchical way. And you can really go on forever with this and map uh and nest one map into the other. Um, and you can also place tokens on it'

[03:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as you can see here. And just like uh you would uh expect, you can also hover over a token and hold down command to see its stop block. Um this is a stat block coming from the 5e SRD just for'

[03:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'demonstration purposes. And it\'s uh imported with fantasy step blocks, which is a plugin that a lot of people already use with an Obsidian for managing their step blocks. And Atlas allows you to'

[04:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just import these and it recognizes any kind of dice. um a syntax and you can just click on that to actually roll the dice. So, for example, if you click on something in a um attribute here called'

[04:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hit points or HP, um it\'ll actually reroll the hit points of that creature, which some people do like for like um old school Essentials games and so on. Um, you can also do the same for attacks'

[04:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and it\'s even going to uh show you the actual name of the feature or action that has taken place within the um dice roll, which I think is kind of handy. You um can also share a map with your'

[04:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'players um by opening up a second window. And this is something that I like to do because I play with um virtual tabletops locally in a sort of hybrid style because I\'m too lazy and'

[04:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'too poor to actually print maps. And so I just uh give them another screen with the digital map on. I think it\'s easier that way and it just makes um preparing'

[05:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'my sessions faster. You can open the um player view by either hitting the space key and then typing in player view and going to um send current map to the player view. You can also go to the um'

[05:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tab in the tab bar and just click on this um I symbol which will open the player view on your second monitor. I have to pull it over. And this player view is just a very minimal view um with'

[05:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'uh dragging enabled everywhere. So, no matter where you click it, you\'ll be able to drag the view around. [music] Um, and it\'ll just replicate what you do on your view so that you don\'t have to'

[05:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'manage a player view um besides your own. And you can also uh determine how the player view should look like. So, you can see right now they had the grid'

